1
00:00:00,670 --> 00:00:14,080
B1 Listen to Lily, a student from grade 9, talking to the Class 1, grade 8 students, about her experience of learning English.

2
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:19,990
Write a T if a sentence is true, or an F if it is false.

3
00:00:19,990 --> 00:00:23,345
Then correct the false ones.

4
00:00:23,345 --> 00:00:27,130
Hi, my name's Lily.

5
00:00:27,130 --> 00:00:29,320
I'm from grade 9.

6
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:33,620
I have some advice on English learning for you.

7
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:38,690
At first, I found learning English really difficult.

8
00:00:38,690 --> 00:00:43,590
But then my teacher gave me some great tips.

9
00:00:43,590 --> 00:00:50,580
First, try to speak English in your daily life as much as possible.

10
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,210
Listen to English songs.

11
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:57,620
Watch TV and films in English.

12
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:02,900
Read English books and speak English often.

13
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:06,170
I also have a language partner.

14
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:11,170
We meet every weekend and speak English for an hour.

15
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:13,970
That really helps.

16
00:01:13,970 --> 00:01:19,820
Second, carry a notebook to help you learn new words.

17
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:27,290
When you come across a new word, write it down and pay attention to its meaning.

18
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:31,760
These tips are some easy ways to improve your English.
